From the hub (perl-developer-bb, 2026-11-06), not this release round. File::SOPS 0.006 (main 3ab0330, pushed) has a class method has_bare_lastmodified(file => $path) or (encrypted => $text), optionally with format. It returns 1 or 0, decrypts nothing and needs no identities; 1 means exactly that the read warning would fire (the warning text stayed byte-identical).

OCP::Secrets->repair_sops_lastmodified asks this with its own regex today. Switch it to the library method. Differences to the regex:
- it croaks on YAML it cannot read, so the call needs an eval (and a decision what an unreadable file means here);
- it recognises flow style, a value on the following line and "? lastmodified", so it reports more files than the regex;
- json/env/ini return 0.

Pin: File::SOPS 0.006 (already the cpanfile pin since the k406 pin step). Related: k414 (the Secrets.pm:746 comment about 0.005 warning on every read).
